# `Char` on the v2 JS lane

Executable record of BUGS.md `js-v2-lane-has-no-Char-at-all` — the v2 JS backend implements
no char primitives, so a char literal and `charAt` both die with `unimplemented primitive`.
The entry carried no gate, so nothing connected the defect to a run.

Both operations are here because the entry names both and they are separate primitives:
a char literal (`char`) and a string index (`scharAt`). A case covering only one would go
green on a half fix.

```scalascript
def main(): Unit =
  println('a')
  val s = "aBc"
  println(s.charAt(1))

main()
```
